					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SMOOTH STEP\n\nThe Smooth Step node does a mathmatical computation normally found in the GLSL language together with its sibling Step.\n\nSmooth Step produces a float value between 0 and 1.\nWhen the incoming value is between its two edges a transition between 0 and 1 starts.\n\nThis can be seen in the example where the right rectangle is the result of the triangle (left rectangle) into the Smooth Step. The middle rectangle is the more absolute version of Smooth Step, called Step."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 226,
					"width": 686,
					"x": 980.392333984375,
					"y": -206.26556396484375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"13": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "OUTLETS\n\n• Main\nOutputs a float that is between 0.0  and 1.0\n\n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
